2. Disk  hub

Everything about storage devices: what's plugged in, how full it is, how it's
mounted.

On your machine
  nvme0n1         476.9 GiB  SSD · Samsung SSD 980 PRO 500GB
    nvme0n1p1     512.0 MiB  vfat   /boot/efi   256.0 MiB free (50%)
    nvme0n1p2     476.4 GiB  btrfs  / (+2)      120.0 GiB free (30%)
    nvme0n1p10      1.0 MiB
  sda              30.0 GiB  rotational · removable · USB DISK 3.0
    (whole disk)             exfat  /media/usb
  zram0             8.0 GiB  SSD · swap
  2 loop or empty devices not shown

Commands
  lsblk                      tree of disks and partitions
  df -h                      free space per mounted filesystem
  du -sh * | sort -h         size of each item here, biggest last
  findmnt                    mount points and their options
  find / -xdev -type f -size +1G 2>/dev/null
                             files over 1 GiB on the root filesystem
  iostat -x 1                live disk activity (package sysstat)
  sudo smartctl -a /dev/sda  disk health (package smartmontools)

Paths
  /dev/disk/by-uuid/     stable names for disks and partitions
  /sys/block/DEV/queue/  I/O scheduler, rotational flag
  /etc/fstab             what gets mounted at boot

Cards
  idk 1.2  /tmp vs /var/tmp
  idk 1.4  Links, inodes and "disk full"
  idk 6.1  find
